[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Asking for Trouble]
[00:12.75]Why did the policeman ask the writer to come to the police station?
[00:21.13]It must have been about two in the morning when I returned home.
[00:26.34]I tried to wake up my wife by ringing the doorbell,
[00:30.24]but she was fast asleep,
[00:32.65]so I got a ladder from the shed in the garden, put it against the wall,
[00:38.63]and began climbing towards the bedroom window.
[00:43.76]I was almost there when a sarcastic voice below said.
[00:49.85]'I don't think the windows need cleaning at this time of the night.'
[00:56.58]I looked down and nearly fell off the ladder when I saw a policeman.
[01:02.03]I immediately regretted answering in the way I did, but I said,'I enjoy cleaning windows at night.'
[01:12.60]'So do I,' answered the policeman in the same tone.
[01:17.88]Excuse my interrupting you.
[01:20.96]I hate to interrupt a man when he's busy working, but would you mind coming with me to the station?'
[01:31.36]'Well, I'd prefer to stay here,' I said.
[01:36.10]'You see, I've forgotten my key.'
[01:39.94]'Your what?' he called.
[01:44.01]'My key,' I shouted.
[01:49.01]Fortunately, the shouting woke up my wife who opened the window just as the policeman had started to climb towards me.
